--
N5008 [class.mem.general]/11, [dcl.init.aggr]/4, [dcl.init.list]/3.7: a
default member initializer `pr tbl[2] = {{'^', t_begin}, {'$', t_end}};'
initializes each array element by list-initialization from its braced
list, calling pr(char, token). The front end found no constructor for the
elements ("found no match for symbol 'pr'", or with std::pair "invalid
implicit conversion from '<<type:>>' to 'struct pair &&'") and dropped the
class's constructor: the NSDMI reached the mem-initializer as ONE braced
list, like `tbl({...})', instead of the list's clauses. This is
libstdc++'s regex _ScannerBase::_M_token_tbl (a const array of
std::pair<char, _TokenT>), so _ScannerBase's constructor
(regex_scanner.h:91) is dropped in 3 regex descs; test_libstdcxx.desc is
that program and forbids only that drop. g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept both
programs. Fails on bin53.
